 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Raíces nuevas en el pasado",
    "@en": "New roots in the past"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**dar** → **dei** (di), **dizer** → **disse** (dije), **vir** → **vim** (vine), **ver** → **vi** (vi), **pôr** → **pus** (puse).",
     "@en": "**dar** → **dei** (di), **dizer** → **disse** (said), **vir** → **vim** (came), **ver** → **vi** (vi), **pôr** → **pus** (put)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "No son las mismas formas que en el presente: **digo** (presente) y **disse** (pasado) son verbos distintos en el tiempo.",
     "@en": "They are not the same forms as in the present: **digo** (present) and **disse** (past) are different verbs in time."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Las terminaciones",
    "@en": "The terminations"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Las terminaciones se parecen a las regulares: **-ste** (tú), **-u** (él o ella), **-mos** (nosotros), **-ram** (ellos).",
     "@en": "The endings are similar to the regular ones: **-ste** (you), **-u** (him or her), **-mos** (us), **-ram** (them)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Ojo: **vim** (vine) y **vieste** (viniste) vienen de **vir**, y **vi** (vi) y **viste** (viste) de **ver**.",
     "@en": "Eye: **vim** (vine) and **vieste** (came) come from **vir**, and **vi** (vi) and **viste** (vestibule) from **ver**."
    }
   ]
  },
